{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788183187,"nonce":"+vG3oCN6Y01yzTR+3VTlsqL0XkE=","message":"VERIFIED GREEN AND MERGED TO MAIN, 2026-08-31, dorian's Linux box.\n109 PASS, 0 FAIL, 2 honest SKIP. Merged fast-forward at 0079e00.\n\nThe acceptance script committed as UNVERIFIED DRAFT (413ab88) needed no\ncorrection — only its exec bit changed. Every expected value in it was right.\n\nTHE REGRESSION TEST IS THE POINT (steps 08-13)\n\nA timing-out letter opens itself from LetterStack.LetterStackTick and stacks a\nforce-pausing dialog. Under 1.3's budgeted DoSingleTick loop we ticked straight\nthrough it and OpenAutomaticLetters was starved for the rest of the session, so\na SECOND timing-out letter would expire in silence.\n\nMeasured under 1.8:\n- first letter halted the advance at its own open tick, 41202 vs 41202\n- dialog cleared, still_force_paused:false\n- SECOND letter arrived and opened, 41801 vs 41801\n\nThat is Evan's argument demonstrated rather than reasoned. The defences I\noffered for the old loop are not merely unpersuasive, they were describing a\nmechanism that actively broke vanilla's own letter timing.\n\nTHE SPEED LADDER, exact — this REPLACES 1.3's tps table\n\n  Normal     nominal  60   measured  59.9857   overshoot bound  2\n  Fast       nominal 180   measured 179.9873   overshoot bound  6\n  Superfast  nominal 360   measured 359.8356   overshoot bound 24\n  Ultrafast  nominal 900   measured 899.7799   overshoot bound 30\n\n20010 ticks in 22.24s wall at Ultrafast. status.json showed paused:false across\n109 samples mid-flight, carrying the in-flight advance block with\nticks_done/target. Pause restored on every exit path exercised: ticks, letter,\ndialog, interrupted. Zero red errors.\n\nAlso confirmed: `until:{letter}` halts on the exact event tick with halted_seq\nnaming the journal line; `max_tps:200` picks Fast and reports max_tps_asked:200,\nmax_tps_clamped.to:180,